      "category": "reasoning",
      "trigger": "When evaluating a pleural effusion in the context of trauma or chest pain to determine etiology.",
      "steps": [
        "Systematically trace the ribs on the side of the effusion, paying close attention to the posterior arcs where fractures are commonly obscured.",
        "Look for cortical discontinuities, step-offs, or callus formation indicating rib fractures.",
        "Correlate the presence of ipsilateral rib fractures with the effusion to support a diagnosis of haemothorax rather than other causes like infection or malignancy."
      ]
    }
  ]
